{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidGroup","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeAlgebra"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.heckeOfBraidRepOfZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.heckeOfBraidRepOfZero","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L149-L153","doc":"The factorisation from the first generator alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.heckeOfBraidRep_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.heckeOfBraidRep_σ","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L143-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.heckeOfBraidRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.heckeOfBraidRep","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L135-L141","doc":"**Factorisation through the Hecke algebra.** A braid representation whose generators are\nall `(s, q, qi)`-Hecke induces a `K`-algebra map `H_m(q) →ₐ[K] A`, `σ_j ↦ s • θ(σ_j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.scaledGen_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.scaledGen_comm","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L127-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.scaledGen_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.scaledGen_braid","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L119-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.scaledGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.scaledGen","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L116-L117","doc":"The scaled generator images `j ↦ s • θ(σ_j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.isHeckeQuad_all_of_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.isHeckeQuad_all_of_zero","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**One generator suffices.** If `θ(σ₀)` is Hecke then every `θ(σ_j)` is: the generators\nare conjugate in the braid group (`σ_succ_eq_conj`) and the condition is\nconjugation-invariant (`isHeckeQuad_conj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.isHeckeQuad_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.isHeckeQuad_conj","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L79-L94","doc":"The Hecke condition is invariant under conjugation by a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.IsHeckeQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.IsHeckeQuad","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L75-L77","doc":"`x` is `(s, q, qi)`-Hecke: `β = s • x` satisfies `β² = (q − qi)β + q·qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.σ_succ_eq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.σ_succ_eq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L62-L65","doc":"**All Artin generators are conjugate.** `σ_{i+1} = w σ_i w⁻¹` with `w = σ_i σ_{i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.σ_comm_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.σ_comm_rel","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L50-L60","doc":"Far commutation `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `i + 2 ≤ j` in `BraidGroup m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.σ_braid_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidHeckeFactor.σ_braid_rel","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidHeckeFactor.lean#L41-L48","doc":"The braid relation `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}` in `BraidGroup m`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}